EXTRA_PROMPT="5. **Champaign County Hyper-Local Analysis** — Isolate and evaluate the specific weather impacts for Champaign County and the immediate East-Central Illinois corridor.\n\nTo perform this analysis, cross-reference the text for explicit mentions of the county or its indirect regional identifiers (e.g., \"East-Central IL\", \"I-57/I-74 corridor\", \"North of I-70\", \"East of the Peoria-Springfield line\", or the aviation identifier **\"KCMI\"**).\n\nStructure this section with these exact bullets:\n* **Relative Risk Tier:** Contrast this specific corridor against the rest of the region. Is the risk for damaging hail, tornadoes, or torrential rain elevated, lower, or baseline compared to surrounding areas? (Note: If the text singles out \"East-Central IL\" or \"KCMI\" for specific hazards like heavy rain or higher storm coverage, the risk here is **elevated**, not equal).\n* **Timing & Meteorological Window:** Extract the exact arrival, peak intensity, and departure windows mentioned for this corridor or the KCMI TAF timeline. \n* **Local Impact Summary:** Translate what these specific regional deviations mean for local infrastructure or travel (e.g., localized flooding on major local routes like I-57/I-74, morning vs. afternoon storm windows). Do not use generic placeholder phrasing."
